(xi)
.to make proposals for determining what degrees, diplomas and other academic distinctions shall be granted by the
University;
(xii)
. to decide what examinations of other Universities may be accepted as equivalent to those of the University and to
negotiate with other Universities for the recognition of the examinations of the University;
(xiii)
. to arrange for the co-ordination of studies and teaching in affiliated colleges and recognized institutions;
(xiv)
. to exercise such other powers and perform such other duties as may be conferred to imposed on it by this Act or the
Statutes, Ordinances, Regulations, Rules, or Bye-laws.

35.
The Statutes.
- Subject to the provisions of this Act, the Statutes may provide for all or any of the following matters, namely:-
(a)
. the powers and duties of the officers of the University, not specifically provided for in this Act;
(b)
. the constitution, powers and duties of the authorities of the University, not specifically provided for in this Act;
(c)
. the procedure for election of members of the Senate, [xxxxxx] the Academic Council and other authorities of the
University and all such other matters relating to these bodies, as may be necessary or desirable to provide;
(cc)
. the procedure for selection and method of appointment, conditions of service, powers and duties of teachers of the
